     | 4 |     noC-File-Listing-Creator (noC-FLC) Version 1.OO     | n |
     l___j               (C)1994 nocTurne deSign/MST               l___j

____________________________.
                            ¦
           O V E R V I E W  |
____________________________| 

 This CLI-based tool allows you  to create a text-file which lists filenames,
 sizes,  dates, and descriptions, given a directory of wares with  FILE_ID's. 
 The  produced  text  is  of ami-express style format and is in chronological
 order,  (ie  the newest files are listed last).  This utility will be useful
 if  you  are  a sysop and lose listings, or are a trader and want to have an
 itemized list of your software, or ... some other reason.
____________________________.
                            ¦
   R E Q U I R E M E N T S  |
____________________________j

   LHA   - (optional) If you intend to be dealing with LHA archives.
   UNZIP - (optional) If you intend to be dealing with ZIP archives.
____________________________.
                            ¦
                 U S A G E  |
____________________________j

 Information is provided within the program if you supply the argument '?' or
 supply  no  arguments  at  all.  This info shall be repeated with more depth
 here:

    Usage:  flc [directory] [textfile] [S|A|D]
     Args:  [directory] - This is the directory whose files will be
                          processed.  All dirs within will be ignored.
             [textfile] - This is where the directory listing will be
                          written to.  If it already exists, the listing
                          will be APPENDED to this file.
                    [S] - This is the default flag: Files will be
                          omitted from the output text if they have
                          no FILE_ID.
                    [A] - This flag will add files without FILE_ID's
                          to the list, but with the description:
                          'Description Unknown'.
                    [D] - You may describe the files with no FILE_ID's
                          yourself, if this flag is set.
                          (The three flags are mutually-exclusive)

    Examples:  flc BBS:newusers/upload BBS:dir1 A
               flc term:downloads term:listings/mywares.txt

 Of  course if you have a lot of files, the process may take a while.  Errors
 will  be  displayed  to  the  console,  AND  will be written to a text file:
 "T:noC-FLC.log".  Aborts by CONTROL-C are supported at any time.
